35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The receipts show two people bought over half the fuel. The mechanic says short runs damage the car faster. We need to account for wear and tear, not just distance.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The other households blamed constant favour-asking. Our own checking phase felt like accusation. We must avoid turning this into surveillance.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The diary confirms the imbalance. Saturdays are triple Tuesdays. The handover state is unacceptable. We need strict, non-negotiable protocols for fuel and cleanliness.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The fixed costs are 280,000 yen. Fuel is lopsided. We need a formula that reflects actual usage, not just equal splits.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The diary shows Saturdays are triple Tuesdays. The checking phase felt like accusation. I’m worried we’ll just repeat that cycle.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Shion, your formula is right. But the mechanic’s warning means short trips cost more. We must price wear, not just fuel.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Daisuke, your worry is justified. The checking phase failed because it felt like policing. We need a system that feels like shared responsibility, not audit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But without strict handover rules, the car remains unusable. We need a checklist, not just goodwill.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Minako, wear is real, but I need the fuel split first. Benjamin, your ""surveillance"" fear is just an excuse to avoid accountability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. I just want to know where the time goes, not who is wrong.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Shion, accountability is necessary, but it must be fair. If we ignore the mechanic’s warning about short trips, we’re just shifting the burden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Shion, accountability without trust is just surveillance. We need a system that feels like shared responsibility, not an audit.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, accountability is necessary, but it must be practical. A checklist ensures the car is actually drivable, not just theoretically available.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, calling it surveillance is weak. The numbers are objective. I’m not auditing people, I’m auditing the car.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I just want to understand the time cost, not assign blame.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
